==Battleground==
*5 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Alpacky]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doremi]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The essence of this stage is to stall and kill Alpacky first to boost income, then hit the enemy base. Lure and eliminate Doremi with Awakened Bahamut Cat before her support catches up, then finish off Kurosawah.

Alpacky's strengthen and survive abilities can actually work in favor of any strategy, as they will likely employ the default [[Cat Cannon]] or [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] to interrupt Doremi's first attack. When Alpacky activates both abilities, she will easily take out anything she hits, but by this point all five Mr. Angels would have spawned already. Once the Cannon eliminates her, players are free to save up and upgrade their [[Worker Cat]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Awakened Bahamut is a fast rusher that delivers rapid and devastating attacks at short range. Though some timing is required, he alone can effectively stunlock Doremi and stop her from attacking. Once Doremi has been slain, Bahamut can also be used against Kurosawah. His [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]] will interfere this stucklock effect by allowing Doremi to be knocked back twice in a single attack: once from Bahamut himself, then again from the Explosion effect, eventually leading to Bahamut's death at the hands of Kurosawa. Therefore, if his Explosion is unlocked, it is advised utilize Attack Up [[Cat Combo]]s in order to mitigate/prevent this effect.
**Level 50 Awakened Bahamut Cats must use [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] (or any other Attack Up M Cat Combo).
**Level 40 Awakened Bahamut Cats are recommended to use one Attack Up (M) combo, and one Attack up (Sm) Cat Combo if available. Otherwise, two Attack Up (Sm) Cat Combos will suffice, although less effective.
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] - Recommended due to their phenomenal performance in The Pure Land, a sufficiently upgraded Manic Island can also be helpful here as a cost-efficient melee attacker to wipe out the initial enemies without draining too much resources.

